{
  "info": {
    "name": "Senderbot — WhatsApp microservice (Adonis) - 2",
    "description": "Bearer-protected WhatsApp REST API. Set `baseUrl` + `internal_api_secret`. Prefer `http://127.0.0.1:PORT` on Windows — `localhost` may resolve to IPv6 (::1) while the app listens on IPv4.\n\n`/sessions/find` and `/sessions/status` return the same snake_case payload: `status`, `valid_session`, `user_info`, `creds_exist`, `is_legacy`, `last_disconnect`, `persisted_on_disk`, `in_memory`. Live `status` comes from Baileys when loaded; DB stores persistence metadata.\n\nEnvelope: `{ success, message, data }` except `/health`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
